ch it is revealed that  they are in fact queer  supernatural or how  immediate from their introduction is it  established that they are dead or we are  forced to witness that they die  star trek discovery but there's another  element that's kind of what i want to  focus on here  and that is the idea of tokenism  which is something i actually haven't  tackled in specific on  this channel before now tokenism  as a practice is is a bad thing now  here's the thing to remember tokenism  is not simply the presence  of minority people in a  story a company an organization what  have you  generally when tokenism is talked about  as say  in a workplace what it refers to is the  practice of hiring  an incredibly small number of  diversity hires i hate using the term  but that is the reality of it  so that it does not appear as if there  is a hiring bias  at that company where the company has  no actual interest and doesn't care  about actually ensuring a diversity  of its work populace or a diversity of  thought  it just knows the it just it's  self-aware enough to know the optics are  really  bad if everybody in the company is  exactly the same  so i'm not trying to pick on on them but  you know if the whole company is  white cis males if you have  at least a woman a person of color  a out queer person in there  then even though only one does not  meaningfully  make them a presence in the organization  it does give a shield  for that organization that employer to  go  oh but look and that one  see it's the appearance  of diversity but it is always  only aiming for the absolute basic  rudimentary appearance of it  now as i said the term kind of  originated more  from employee and hiring practices  now when talking about it in terms of  entertainment  and media tokenism is a thing  and when it happens it is often  damaging for the groups being  represented now i say that as someone  who has said in the past and i stand by  this  i would rather have problematic  representation 