nly got the one  representation  but that's kind of why  my answer to should queer characters be  immortal is a soft yes  is this exact reason i've known it  before i did a video  on uh mortality rates for queer  characters in film  it's not just that we get killed  in a lot of movies tv shows books comics  etc  it's that when we do we  we as a queer audience  often have to watch the  queer character die our  soul representative of our life  experience  is who we have to watch die  or often times even when that isn't the  case  and there's more than one usually  they're a couple  and we have to watch one half of a  couple die so we're still looking at a  50  mortality rate with the remaining 50 now  in mourning and it  feels like an attack  when you watch it often enough and i'm  even gonna extend an olive branch  to a kind of viewer who probably has not  watched this far into the video  if we're being completely honest but i'm  gonna try it anyway  you folks who have been complaining  about doctor who  the last few series you know who you are  the ones who have been commenting and my  comments other people's comments  possibly been making videos about  how every single straight white male who  appears  in the chibnall and jodie whitaker era  of doctor who  is shown to be an idiot or a villain  there are no competent  righteous good straight  white male characters on doctor who i  know you complain about and i'm not  i'm not even gonna run the numbers to  find out how true that is because  honestly  how true it is in reality is irrelevant  to what i'm about to say  if you have ever felt that way at any  point even if you don't feel that way  now  if you ever felt that way then you  got a taste  of what it feels like to have  every instance of representation that  you see that looks like you  feel negative either because they are  depicted as villainous  or as stereotypes or because they are  getting  killed every time  you see them and again it probably isn't  actua